{"name":"Cerulean Frost","hex":"#6d9bc3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cerulean","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A greenish-blue color.","Any of various lycaenid butterflies of the genus Jamides."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sky-blue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cerulean"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cerulean","blocks":[{"text":"The color cerulean, or caerulean, is a variety of the hue of blue that may range from a light azure blue to a more intense sky blue. Cerulean may also be mixed with the hue of green. The first recorded use of cerulean as a color name in English was in 1590. The word is derived from the Latin word caeruleus, \"dark blue, blue, or blue-green\", which in turn probably derives from caerulum, diminutive of caelum, \"heaven, sky\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerulean"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/250px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/500px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/250px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Cerulean_blue_hue.png/250px-Cerulean_blue_hue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/Cerulean_blue_hue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Cerulean_blue_hue.png/250px-Cerulean_blue_hue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACerulean_blue_hue.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Ceruleum.png/250px-Ceruleum.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Ceruleum.png/500px-Ceruleum.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Ceruleum.png/250px-Ceruleum.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeruleum.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Cerulean_warbl